Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:41.11,Hdr,,0,0,0,,May 19, 1968 - Satsuki Sho
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Past the 400 mark, Kadomasu is hanging on along the rail
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.20,0:00:06.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,Takeshiba O comes through the middle - will he take the lead?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.40,0:00:09.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,And out wide, Asaka O and Marchs are coming up together
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.80,0:00:12.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Just under 200 metres to the finish
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:13.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,The three leaders are now side by side
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.90,0:00:15.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Here it is - will it be the warrior Takeshiba O?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.50,0:00:16.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,The chestnut Marchs?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.90,0:00:19.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Or the blue-blooded prince, Asaka O?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.20,0:00:21.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Three horses locked in a three-way battle
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.80,0:00:23.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,You could call this the clash of the Big Three
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.80,0:00:25.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,Marchs just edging ahead on the outside
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.90,0:00:32.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Marchs in front - and he wins it!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.00,0:00:33.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,The winner is Marchs
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.60,0:00:36.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,First leg of the Classics - Marchs takes a fierce fight
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.50,0:00:39.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two-year-old champion Takeshiba O fights for second